WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.200
We’re all familiar with viral diseases,
especially over the past two years.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:11.440
The deadliness and severity of a virus cannot
be understated, whether it’s COVID-19, influenza,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.210
or any other of the countless infectious diseases
that plague humanity.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.960
We’re all familiar with the bubonic plague,
the black death which wiped out an estimated

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:25.390
25 million people in the middle ages, a third
of Europe’s population at the time.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:29.939
But that was during an era in which medical
advances were limited to the sickening practice

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:34.410
of bloodletting, which drained a patient of
their blood until all bacteria left their

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.140
system, or washing the body with vinegar.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.840
Of course, none of these methods had any effect
in staving off the Black Death, and the epidemic

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.930
went down in history as one of the darkest
periods of civilization.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:51.010
But for all our technological and medical
advances in the field of health and medicine,

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.960
infectious diseases are still as much of a
threat now as they were back then, if not

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.060
a greater one.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.240
Think about it, in today’s world, everything
is heavily connected.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:06.140
Globalization means that we travel more, import
more products than ever before, and with such

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.229
a high population density, it’s difficult
to keep anything under control due to the

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:13.009
sheer amount of people there are in the world.

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:17.909
Complete eradication of a viral disease has
proven extremely difficult in even the strictest,

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:20.329
most regimented campaigns to do so.

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:25.320
Vaccines, while effective, still require time
to develop, roll out, and treat.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.329
Take for example the Smallpox virus.

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:32.130
For centuries, this deadly disease slayed
entire populations, killing millions with

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.600
a mortality rate of 40%.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.880
In the 20th century, the world’s governments
and medical organizations worked tirelessly

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.670
to come up with a vaccinated cure for the
disease, and their efforts eventually paid

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.670
off.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.799
A successful vaccine was developed, and only
the trinkling of cases of smallpox were documented

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:51.920
in Somalia in the 1970s.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.009
Today, all that remains of the disease are
contained samples held in high-security laboratories

00:01:57.009 --> 00:02:01.279
across the world, explicitly used for research
purposes.

00:02:01.279 --> 00:02:04.600
But Smallpox’s story is not the norm.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.780
Other diseases you may not realize are still
lurking in the shadows are polio and malaria.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.260
Polio being a disease affecting the central
nervous system, with weakened muscle function

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:20.310
as a result, and Malaria being a mosquito-transmitted
sickness that results in severe fevers and

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.310
vomiting.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:25.260
The common perception is that these illnesses
aren’t actually a threat anymore, and are

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.879
nothing more than a relic of the past, but
that isn’t quite true.

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:33.320
While they’ve been eliminated from some
parts of the world, in Polio’s case, most

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:38.370
first world countries such as the United States
and Europe, still have some documented cases

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.450
that crop up from time to time.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:45.400
But the future is hopeful, with only under
50 cases of polio documented worldwide in

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:51.520
the year 2018, and Malaria’s worldwide eradication
programs seeing success year by year, maybe

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.630
the world will one day be fully wiped of these
terrible illnesses.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.920
But why are we telling you this during a video
about the SCP Foundation?

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.780
Because the subject of today’s video is
also a deadly virus, but unlike the more ordinary

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.680
variations we just discussed, this one is
going to be a lot more difficult to eradicate

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.680
fully.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.659
And by difficult, we mean next to impossible.

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:18.780
As to be expected with an organization like
the SCP Foundation, the threats they deal

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.110
with are both similar to the ones the rest
of the world’s governments and large organizations

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:26.150
do, and entirely, completely different.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.629
If you’re a seasoned viewer of SCP Explained,
chances are you’re already familiar with

00:03:30.629 --> 00:03:33.010
more than a few anomalous viruses.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:38.340
They’re unspeakably deadly, incredibly strange,
and can put an infected victim through more

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.020
pain and suffering than anything else in the
world.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:45.629
It’s a testament to the Foundation’s thoroughness
and capabilities that some of these diseases

00:03:45.629 --> 00:03:51.500
are even able to be concentrated in a manageable
dose and contained inside a chamber at a secure

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.540
facility.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:57.159
But for others, they’re still out there,
ready to strike at a moment’s notice, and

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:02.099
there’s absolutely nothing the Foundation
can do about it except be as swift as possible

00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:03.910
in their retaliation.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.280
And there’s no doubt that they’re prepared.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:10.489
With the deadliness of an anomalous virus,
which can spread at a more infectious rate

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:14.900
and potentially alert the rest of the world
to the supernatural happenings of the SCP

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:20.250
Foundation and the objects they contain, an
anomalous pandemic is one of the Foundation’s

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.750
greatest fears.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:26.319
Some anomalous diseases, as we mentioned before,
are under the control of the Foundation.

00:04:26.319 --> 00:04:31.180
Take SCP-008, nicknamed the Zombie Plague,
for example.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:36.470
SCP-008 is a deadly virus that, you guessed
it, can essentially turn a patient into a

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:40.419
zombie, reanimating their corpse after the
sickness kills them.

00:04:40.419 --> 00:04:45.840
What makes SCP-008 unique is that it’s entirely
absent from the natural world, save for the

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.710
places the Foundation has labeled “G2 Sites”.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:55.750
These G2 Sites are small pockets across the
world in which the Foundation discovered SCP-008,

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.889
which further research of such have determined
that the disease may not have originated on

00:04:59.889 --> 00:05:01.930
earth in the first place.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:07.210
Subjects infected by SCP-008 display symptoms
within three hours of infection, which include

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:11.470
flu-like symptoms preceded by a coma, which
is followed by death.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:17.060
But after death, the victim’s body will
continue to display lifeless signs of mortality,

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:21.680
including a high durability to damage and
a desire to ingest living humans on physical

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.100
contact.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.780
Just like a zombie.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:30.500
Research into SCP-008 is highly classified
and left out from the original document, because

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:36.169
the Foundation has the right to fear that
SCP-008 may be replicated in an unsuspecting

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.900
laboratory one day.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.540
As such, containment efforts to prevent such
research from bearing fruit are in place,

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:46.780
backed by the Foundation’s stranglehold
over the ordinary scientific world.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:53.000
Thankfully, SCP-008 has mostly been destroyed,
with samples contained solely at the G2 sites,

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:57.350
which are now protected Foundation facilities,
located across the world.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:02.020
But the Foundation was lucky that SCP-008
was so easily contained.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:06.349
If the disease spread in larger numbers, or
originated from a natural source on earth,

00:06:06.349 --> 00:06:11.139
we might be living in a world more like a
zombie apocalypse movie than the one we know

00:06:11.139 --> 00:06:12.139
today.

00:06:12.139 --> 00:06:16.940
On the other side of the spectrum, you have
SCP-3519, the “Quiet Days” virus.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:22.819
In one reality, SCP-3519 managed to kill off
the entire world, due to its severity and

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:24.500
ease of infection.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:30.480
Unlike most anomalous diseases, SCP-3519 was
a memetic virus, meaning that its transmission

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.930
wasn’t just limited to the traditional means
of physical contact, but the very idea of

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:39.770
it permeating your mind would allow it to
take root inside your body.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:46.150
SCP-3519 permeated the idea that the world
would end on March 5th, 2019, and that self-termination

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:50.430
was a preferable option than living through
the apocalypse and the terrible aftermath

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.100
that would follow.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:58.110
SCP-3519 took society by storm, and the idea
was transmitted through television broadcasts

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:03.330
and news stories encouraging people to free
themselves from the world, and even Foundation

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:05.199
sites themselves.

00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:09.440
The Foundation was powerless, and the rapid
rate of transmission proved too difficult

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.539
for the organization to keep fully under control.

00:07:12.539 --> 00:07:16.919
The project to create a cure was greenlit,
but one by one, as Foundation sites across

00:07:16.919 --> 00:07:21.760
the globe suffered massive die-offs and a
loss of personnel, the research team dwindled

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:27.330
down until there was only one person left,
a junior researcher by the name of Rory Jones,

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:33.229
who assumed the position of O5-6 in an emergency
succession protocol that would promote the

00:07:33.229 --> 00:07:38.139
next highest member of the Foundation to the
position in the event of an Overseer dying.

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:42.659
Jones was the only member of the Foundation
left, and as far as he knew, camped up in

00:07:42.659 --> 00:07:47.580
a cabin in the woods with nothing but a few
research materials and a computer terminal,

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.610
the only man alive.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:55.379
The SCP-3519 timeline’s story proves just
how quickly a deadly anomalous virus can get

00:07:55.379 --> 00:07:56.379
out of control.

00:07:56.379 --> 00:08:01.760
How it can make an organization as all-powerful
and ever-prepared as the SCP Foundation just

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.770
another statistic in a record of infected
populations.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:09.889
But you don’t need to tell the Foundation
that, they’re already well aware, and they’ve

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:14.770
had decades to prepare, study, and analyze
the effect an anomalous virus can have on

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:15.770
the world.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:19.699
And that brings us to the mysterious case
of the main anomaly we’ll be looking at

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.270
today:

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.990
SCP-217 - The Clockwork Virus.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:28.919
Dr. Charles Gears, a researcher of note that
you may have heard of before, was one of the

00:08:28.919 --> 00:08:30.730
Foundation’s best and brightest.

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:35.729
His cold, distant demeanor and propensity
for researching the anomalous commonly associated

00:08:35.729 --> 00:08:40.390
with the divergent religion, the Church of
the Broken God, a group of zealots focused

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:45.280
on reassembling the broken, metal pieces of
their mechanical, technological god, made

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:52.220
onlookers associate the Gears name with sleek,
careless alloys, and methodical, cold clockwork.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:56.821
When the Foundation began observing symptoms
of what would later be labeled SCP-217 in

00:08:56.821 --> 00:09:01.530
a major population center whose name would
be scrubbed from all official documents, they

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:05.610
knew Dr. Gears was the right man to head the
research efforts.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:10.690
For years, the Foundation had observed strange
medical records and reports from the city.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:15.130
Reports of dementia in subjects younger than
the common age brackets and at an uncommonly

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.540
high rate.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:21.540
High reports of lethargy, depression, emotional
dulling, and a feeling of something moving

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:26.290
underneath the skin, or a ticking noise in
the ear, were all signs that the Foundation

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.370
was dealing with SCP-217.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:33.730
Dr. Gears was already familiar with the disease,
having worked alongside efforts to study it

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:35.010
in the past.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:40.300
This was not the first major population area
affected by SCP-217, and there surely were

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.400
more areas up next.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:47.190
Upon arriving and reading the initial reports,
Dr. Gears requested to view a subject that

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:51.100
the Foundation believed was suffering from
SCP-217.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:55.180
When the young woman entered, Gears immediately
recognized the signs.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:10:00.280
The stiff movements, the robotic, monotone
voice, and the way that nothing he seemed

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.790
to say phased her.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:06.200
They were all clear cut signs of SCP-217’s
infection.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:10.690
The girl was barely high school age, but she
looked like she had all of her youth and life

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.750
sapped from her completely.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.269
It was a horrible sight to see.

00:10:15.269 --> 00:10:20.770
An X-Ray was performed, and Gears saw for
himself a definitive sign that SCP-217 had

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.420
taken over her body.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:26.660
The X-Ray imagery showed the inside of the
girl’s body, which had been converted from

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:33.529
an ordinary mass of organs and tissues into
a clockwork machine, composed of cogs, gears,

00:10:33.529 --> 00:10:35.260
screws, and wires.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:40.360
And as Gears knew, this would only get worse
as time went on, with signs of her infection

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.709
appearing outside the body as well as inside.

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:48.170
Right now, there wasn’t a shred of human
tissue left inside her, and there was nothing

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:50.430
the doctor could do about it.

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:54.410
Gears thought about the girl’s family, who
had been amnesticized prior to the Foundation

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:58.910
seizing their daughter for research purposes,
and though the emotionless man would never

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:02.700
let his facade down, on the inside his heart
ached for her.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:07.160
But it wasn’t only her, it was dozens of
people inside the city the Foundation had

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.360
documented as displaying symptoms of SCP-217.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:16.890
On a scale this high, there was little the
Foundation could do except sit back, watch,

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:20.440
and only act when the symptoms became too
visible to hide.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:24.790
That was the tragedy of SCP-217, the clockwork
virus.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:29.880
It wasn’t deadly, but it was a slow, more
metaphorical death, from a person made of

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:35.480
flesh and blood, to a clockwork automaton
that felt more like a shell than a living

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:36.480
thing.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:41.389
The Foundation was more than familiar with
SCP-217 though, and multiple samples are held

00:11:41.389 --> 00:11:45.980
inside a reverse-pressure airlocked containment
chamber at a high security site for research

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:50.640
purposes, in hopes that one day a cure could
be developed.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.290
Personnel wanting to access SCP-217 samples
have to don fully insulated hazmat suits,

00:11:56.290 --> 00:12:01.329
with chemical sterilization and endure a
post-interaction quarantine period, with physical

00:12:01.329 --> 00:12:02.329
testing.

00:12:02.329 --> 00:12:06.690
All this being mandatory after they have finished
their experiments with the virus.

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:12.630
The severity of an SCP-217 infection can not
be understated, and any items touched by infected

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.589
personnel have to undergo a strict sterilization
process.

00:12:16.589 --> 00:12:22.480
The Foundation is perfectly justified in this
overly cautious behavior too, because SCP-217

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:28.079
has an infection rate of 100%, meaning that
it will transmit through physical contact

00:12:28.079 --> 00:12:31.120
all of the time, without failure.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:37.170
But it doesn’t just infect humans, the clockwork
virus has been observed to infect all multicellular

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.170
organisms.

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:44.860
From the smallest insect to an elephant, SCP-217
consumes and hollows out all it can.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:49.370
Clockwork beings wrought from a clockwork
virus, marching to the ticking of their innards

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.590
in a hollow, empty world.

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:56.959
If that sounds terrifying and like a nightmare,
then congratulations, chances are you’re

00:12:56.959 --> 00:12:59.510
unaffected by SCP-217.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:04.010
If it sounds appealing, well, you might just
be a Mekhanite ready to serve the Church of

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.010
the Broken God.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.410
But we’ll get to that connection later.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:11.459
SCP-217 is especially difficult to deal with
due to its hardiness.

00:13:11.459 --> 00:13:16.959
It can survive for years outside a host body,
and when it does find a suitable host, and

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:21.750
trust us, there’s no shortage in supply
of them in the world, it can sometimes take

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:25.480
years for symptoms of SCP-217 to manifest.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:30.000
It’s a slow virus, and that’s exactly
what makes it so dangerous.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:35.480
The Foundation might not realize a large population
area has been infected before its too late,

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:41.610
and that’s exactly what happened before,
with entire towns being infected by SCP-217.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:43.220
But what are those symptomes?

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:48.670
Well, you might have been able to guess so
far that SCP-217 has to do with turning someone

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:54.180
into a mechanical monstrosity, but there’s
a bit more to it than that.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:14:00.630
SCP-217 alters bio-chemistry in such a way
that causes organic matter to re-arrange itself

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.700
into an organic metal.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:07.759
Chemical scans of this metal reveal that there’s
still living, cellular tissue and DNA present

00:14:07.759 --> 00:14:13.570
inside it, but it takes the appearance and
feels indistinguishable from actual materials.

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:18.360
This process occurs slowly over time, and
advanced stages have shown that a subject’s

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:23.680
interior will resemble a machine, with a complicated
mixture of gears and clockwork.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:29.480
This is subtle, barely noticed by the patient
at first, with only vague feelings of confusion,

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:34.630
insomnia, and joint stiffness, but as larger
and larger parts of the body are converted,

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.500
the subject experiences extreme pain.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:42.899
As Dr. Gears wrote in his research notes on
SCP-217: “Hearts are replaced by gears and

00:14:42.899 --> 00:14:48.720
small tubes, joints by gear networks, eyes
by structures not unlike primitive “hand-crank”

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.910
film cameras, etc.”

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:55.230
SCP-217, in non-mammals, shows first on the
outside of the body.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:15:00.720
In mammals, such as humans, SCP-217 converts
the internals before being visible on the

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.389
outside of the body.

00:15:02.389 --> 00:15:06.610
The reason for this is unknown, but it might
have something to do with that Broken God

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:08.720
connection we mentioned earlier.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:13.790
One of the Church’s core beliefs focus on
‘ascending’ humanity to reflect Mekhane,

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:14.790
the Broken God.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:20.160
While the origins of SCP-217 are unknown,
if the virus is related to the Mekhanites,

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:25.709
this subtle, slow infection may be a part
of their grand design, a plan to covertly

00:15:25.709 --> 00:15:30.360
infiltrate society and convert the masses
into effigies of their god.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.420
But of course, this is all speculation.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:39.110
As we mentioned, those infected by SCP-217
can be entirely unaware of their conversion

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:41.000
until it’s too late.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:45.250
But aside from physicality, the mental state
is also affected.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:51.130
From the middle to advanced stages of SCP-217
infection, victims' behaviors reflect their

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.829
cold, mechanical insides.

00:15:52.829 --> 00:15:57.010
They respond in a repetitive, disassociated
fashion.

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.220
Their actions are dull, mechanical, and telegraphed.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:05.090
They’re easily distracted and confused,
and appear irritable when faced with new problems.

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:12.540
In the early stages, SCP-217 manifests as
increased lethargy, a lack of emotional response,

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.630
and a feeling of “fluttering” or “moving”
underneath the skin.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:23.200
Always present are ticking noises, like those
of a clock, that mainly manifest when SCP-217

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:25.850
infects the shoulders, neck, and head.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:30.769
But attempts to hear this noise using recording
equipment have invariably failed, as the device

00:16:30.769 --> 00:16:34.589
will not pick up any sound if pressed against
an affected area.

00:16:34.589 --> 00:16:40.660
As SCP-217’s infection advances, the subject
will experience excruciating pain.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:46.209
Sharp, tearing sensations in the areas that
are being converted into organic metal, comparable

00:16:46.209 --> 00:16:49.630
in feeling to a knife wound or a deep muscle
tear.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:54.010
This feeling can persist for hours or days,
depending on which area of the body is being

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:56.730
affected and the subject themselves.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:17:01.579
After tearing the existing organs, the new
parts will integrate into the tissue and settle

00:17:01.579 --> 00:17:03.920
into the body, producing pain.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:09.310
An analysis of this newly formed organic metal
appear to be alloys of the brass, steel, and

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:14.990
iron varieties, but substances such as leather,
rubber, glass, and wood have been observed.

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:20.640
And observed is the key word, because as soon
as these materials are examined deeper, it’s

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:26.550
revealed that they’re still organic in composition,
and even carry the subject’s DNA.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:30.000
Organs and tissues affected will, however,
become stronger.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.061
Instead of being squishy meat-bags filled
with tissue, blood, and other parts, they

00:17:34.061 --> 00:17:39.230
take on the physical properties, namely durability,
of the material they resemble.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:44.650
If one of these areas are damaged, they’ll
repair over time, just like regular organs,

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:46.200
but at a much slower rate.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:51.500
But one interesting note is that a damaged
piece of organic metal can be repaired, so

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:56.280
to speak, by replacing damaged areas with
new parts of the same type.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:18:00.690
This has had no consequences, and the body
will continue to act as normal.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:06.060
That’s one benefit of being infected by
SCP-217, you can essentially repair yourself

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.750
with whatever you have access to.

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:13.230
But the conversion of a victim doesn’t stop,
it continues to occur until their entire body

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:16.630
is organic metal, inside and out.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:21.410
Dr. Gears’ research on a fully converted
brain was apparently so ground-breaking that

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:25.430
it had to be erased from the standard security
class documentation.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:28.140
We can only speculate on what it contained.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:31.500
Possibly that connection to the Broken God
that we’re so desperate to make?

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:36.630
We don’t know, but whatever it was, it hinted
at something far larger than what a cursory

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:40.600
look at SCP-217 seems to suggest.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:45.200
SCP-217 is truly one of the most dangerous
anomalous viruses the Foundation has to deal

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:49.890
with, having already infected hundreds of
people in various population centers around

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:53.900
the world before containment methods can be
properly established.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:58.750
So if you happen to start hearing the sounds
of a tick here and a tock there, accompanied

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:03.420
by a strange fluttering feeling under your
skin, we’re sorry to say, there’s not

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:05.750
much we can do for you now.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:06.750
Actually nothing.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.480
There’s nothing we can do.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:15.670
Now go check out “SCP-914 - The Clockworks”
and “SCP-001 - The Broken God - Ouroboros

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.780
Cycle” for more Mekhanite related videos
from SCP Explained!

